<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.12.5: Identifying Graphs of Quadratic Equations</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01955</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.12.5: Identifying Graphs of Quadratic Equations</md:title>
    <md:uuid>b037e657-a260-4ca8-8258-f77df075fcac</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001"><title>Cool Down</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Here are graphs that represent three quadratic functions, defined by:</para>
      <para id="para-00002"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00016"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00017"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00003">
          <media alt="Graph of three parabolas on a coordinate plane. The x-axis extends from negative 5 to 5 with a scale of 1. The y-axis extends from negative 8 to 10 with a scale of 2. The green parabola is labeled function A. The blue parabola is labeled function B. The black parabola is labeled function C.">
            <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_14_12_01.svg"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>

        <exercise id="_200d8791-5375-4d74-8a94-8d7d0b9bad61" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00004">Which graph represents the equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00005">Correct! Blue Graph B because the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and the graph opens upward.</para>
            <para id="para-00006">Incorrect. The correct answer is Blue Graph B because the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and the graph opens upward.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="cd497fb3-7b75-4099-a3c2-2278ada45ded" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            <para id="para-00007">Which graph represents the equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00008">Correct! Black Graph C because the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and the graph opens downward.</para>
            <para id="para-00009">Incorrect. The correct answer is Black Graph C because the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and the graph opens downward.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_5007f1e3-3da1-4798-a4ba-f8447ef38153" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00003">
            <para id="para-00010">Which graph represents the equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            <para id="para-00011">Correct! Green Graph A because the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and the graph opens upward.</para>
            <para id="para-00012">Incorrect. The correct answer is Green Graph A because the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and the graph opens upward.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

      <!--
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset-problem" data-problem-comparator="text" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="-x^2">
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-problem-content">
    <ol class="os-raise-noindent">
      <li>Which part of the equation tells us that Graph C opens downward?</li>
    </ol>
  
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-correct-response">
    <p>Correct! The negative coefficient of \(x^2\) makes the graph open downward.</p>
  
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-attempts-exhausted-response">

  

-->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00013">Which part of the equation tells us that Graph C opens downward?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          
          <para id="para-00014">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00015"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> is the equation. The negative coefficient of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> makes the graph open downward.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content></document>
